  "root_cause": "Both outer services run under systemd-run --wait --pipe --collect. The command records termination before EXIT trap unconditionally calls systemctl stop on the collected service. That redundant stop reports not-loaded exit 5.",
  "independent_failure": "EXIT trap records cleanup_status but exits only original_status. In both lifeline lanes original_status=0 masks cleanup_status=5. Native campaign original_status=1 remains failed for its own original acceptance failure.",
  "authority_boundary": "The fixed-parent root lease authorizes only trnmponpublic.slice and derived probe slice. It is not authority for either outer .service. Name uniqueness/comment alone is not proof authorizing a stop after StartTransientUnit failed or name was reused.",
  "evidence_limit": "Pinned artifacts prove service terminal messages and manager not-loaded errors, but do not retain a post-cleanup manager+kernel-cgroup absence observation for the two outer services. Fixed-parent pids.current=0/populated=0 and owned runtime slice removal do not close that distinct outer-service gap.",
  "minimal_candidate": {
